            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $h(t)=e^{-2t}u(t)$, rewrite $h(t-\\tau)$ when the output time is fixed at $t=4$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "$h(4-\\tau)=e^{-2(4-\\tau)}u(4-\\tau)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The fixed output time is $t=4$, so substitute $4$ only for $t$ in the argument $t-\\tau$ and leave $\\tau$ as the variable.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "t-\\tau \\quad \\longrightarrow \\quad 4-\\tau",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Now replace the input of $h(\\cdot)$ with $4-\\tau$, giving $h(4-\\tau)=e^{-2(4-\\tau)}u(4-\\tau)$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "free-response",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $h(t)=e^{-3t}u(t)$, rewrite $h(t-\\tau)$ when the output time is fixed at $t=2$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "$h(2-\\tau)=e^{-3(2-\\tau)}u(2-\\tau)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The fixed output time is $t=2$. In $h(t-\\tau)$, substitute $2$ for $t$ but keep $\\tau$ as the varying integration variable.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "t-\\tau \\quad \\longrightarrow \\quad 2-\\tau",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Using the formula for $h$, the argument $2-\\tau$ replaces the input of both factors, so $h(2-\\tau)=e^{-3(2-\\tau)}u(2-\\tau)$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 3,
        "lesson_title": "Holding $t$ Fixed During Convolution",
        "section_index": 3,
        "section_title": "Forming $x(\\tau)h(t-\\tau)$ with $t$ Fixed",
        "step_type": "example",
        "question_type": "free-response",
        "answer_cardinality": "single",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "question_count": 2,
        "questions": [
          {
            "question_index": 1,
            "question_type": "free-response",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Given $x(\\tau)=2\\tau u(\\tau)$ and $h(t)=e^{-3t}u(t)$, form $x(\\tau)h(t-\\tau)$ for fixed output time $t=1$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "$2\\tau u(\\tau)e^{-3(1-\\tau)}u(1-\\tau)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Keep $x(\\tau)$ as a function of $\\tau$. Substitute the fixed value $t=1$ only into the impulse-response factor, so $h(t-\\tau)$ becomes $h(1-\\tau)$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "x(\\tau)h(1-\\tau)=2\\tau u(\\tau)e^{-3(1-\\tau)}u(1-\\tau)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "free-response",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Given $x(\\tau)=4\\tau u(\\tau)$ and $h(t)=e^{-2t}u(t)$, form $x(\\tau)h(t-\\tau)$ for fixed output time $t=3$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "$4\\tau u(\\tau)e^{-2(3-\\tau)}u(3-\\tau)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The input factor is already $x(\\tau)$, so do not substitute $t=3$ into it. Use $3-\\tau$ as the argument of $h$ and multiply the two factors.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "x(\\tau)h(3-\\tau)=4\\tau u(\\tau)e^{-2(3-\\tau)}u(3-\\tau)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 3,
        "lesson_title": "Holding $t$ Fixed During Convolution",
        "section_index": 4,
        "section_title": "Comparing the Integrand for Different Fixed Values of $t$",
        "step_type": "example",
        "question_type": "free-response",
        "answer_cardinality": "single",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "question_count": 2,
        "questions": [
          {
            "question_index": 1,
            "question_type": "free-response",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $x(\\tau)=\\tau u(\\tau)$ and $h(t)=u(t)$, form and compare $x(\\tau)h(t-\\tau)$ for fixed output times $t=2$ and $t=5$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "For $t=2$, $x(\\tau)h(2-\\tau)=\\tau u(\\tau)u(2-\\tau)$. For $t=5$, $x(\\tau)h(5-\\tau)=\\tau u(\\tau)u(5-\\tau)$. Only the fixed output-time value inside the impulse-response factor changes; $x(\\tau)$ stays the same.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Form a separate integrand for each fixed output time. The input factor stays $\\tau u(\\tau)$ in both cases, and the unit-step argument in $h(t-\\tau)$ changes with the fixed value of $t$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\nx(\\tau)h(2-\\tau)&=\\tau u(\\tau)u(2-\\tau)\\\\\nx(\\tau)h(5-\\tau)&=\\tau u(\\tau)u(5-\\tau)\n\\end{aligned}",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "free-response",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "For $x(\\tau)=3u(\\tau)$ and $h(t)=e^{-2t}u(t)$, form and compare $x(\\tau)h(t-\\tau)$ for fixed output times $t=1$ and $t=4$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "For $t=1$, $x(\\tau)h(1-\\tau)=3e^{-2(1-\\tau)}u(\\tau)u(1-\\tau)$. For $t=4$, $x(\\tau)h(4-\\tau)=3e^{-2(4-\\tau)}u(\\tau)u(4-\\tau)$. Only the fixed value in the impulse-response factor changes; the input factor remains $3u(\\tau)$.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
